.TH mnnn-org-cert-acme 1  "mnnn-org-cert-acme 2.11.2" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-org\-cert\-acme \- Set up ACME (Let\*(Aqs Encrypt), or turn it off with \-\-off
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn org cert acme\fR [\fB\-\-domain\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-http\-port\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-off\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set up ACME (Let\*(Aqs Encrypt), or turn it off with \-\-off
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-domain\fR \fI<DOMAIN>\fR
The public name the certificate is for (it must point at this machine)
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Contact address given to the CA
.TP
\fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIRECTORY>\fR
letsencrypt, letsencrypt\-staging or a directory URL
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Certificate profile (shortlived; an empty value for the CA\*(Aqs default)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-http\-port\fR \fI<HTTP_PORT>\fR
Port the HTTP\-01 challenge is answered on
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-off\fR
Turn ACME off (back to self\-signed certificates)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.11.2
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
